        - Use only the provided context.\n                    - Do not invent facts.\n                    - Every bullet MUST copy the citation label EXACTLY as shown in the evidence, including the square brackets.\n                        Correct example:\n                          [sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | table]\n\n                        Incorrect examples:\n                          sample_report_p2_c0\n                          sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf\n\n                        - Prefer compression over completeness.\n                        - Do not restate the same evidence twice.\n                        - If evidence is incomplete, say so briefly.\n                        - Keep the full response under 220 words.\n                        - Use short bullets, not long paragraphs.\n      ", "user_prompt": "\n                      User Question:\n                      What evidence-backed recommendations should management act on immediately?\n\n                      Structured Evidence:\n                      === EXECUTIVE_OVERVIEW ===\n- [sample_report_p1_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview]\nQuarterly Strategic Review — Northstar Retail\nGroup\nSample leadership report for testing a PDF → extraction → chunking → retrieval → executive-summary\npipeline\n1. Executive Overview\nNorthstar Retail Group closed Q2 FY2026 with revenue of $128.4M, up 11.7% year over year, driven by\nstrong digital channel growth and improved premium-category conversion. Gross margin expanded to\n38.6% from 36.9% in the prior-year quarter, supported by lower freight costs and better inventory mix.\nHowever, management noted emerging pressure in same-store traffic across Tier-2 locations and higher\ncustomer acquisition costs in paid media.\nLeadership should view the quarter as operationally solid but strategically mixed: the company is\ndemonstrating resilience in e-commerce and private-label performance, while store productivity and\nmarketing efficiency remain the principal watch areas for the next two quarters.\n2. Performance Summary\nMetric\nQ2 FY2025\nQ2 FY2026\nYoY Change\nRevenue ($M)\n114.9\n128.4\n+11.7%\nGross Margin\n36.9%\n38.6%\n+170 bps\nOperating Income ($M)\n12.2\n15.8\n+29.5%\nDigital Revenue Mix\n29.4%\n35.1%\n+570 bps\nCustomer Acquisition Cost ($)\n18.7\n22.4\n+19.8%\nInventory Days\n74\n61\n-13 days\n3. Segment Commentary\nDigital Commerce. Online sales grew 34% year over year, led by repeat purchase behavior in home\norganization and wellness categories. Management attributed the acceleration to improved product\nrecommendation models, mobile checkout simplification, and faster fulfillment SLAs in metro regions.\nPhysical Stores. Store revenue increased only 2%, with strong flagship performance partly offset by\nweaker traffic in smaller-format suburban stores. Basket size improved, but footfall declined 5% in Tier-2\nlocations, suggesting that conversion is improving faster than raw demand.\nPrivate Label. Private-label penetration reached 21% of revenue versus 16% a year earlier. This mix shift\nwas margin-accretive and reduced exposure to third-party pricing volatility.\n4. Strategic Risks and Opportunities\nCategory\nObservation\nImplication\nRisk\nPaid media CAC increased nearly 20% YoY\nGrowth may become less efficient unless\nacquisition mix shifts toward retention and\norganic demand\n\n\n=== LEADERSHIP_QUESTIONS ===\n- [sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions]\nRisk\nTier-2 store traffic declined 5%\nStore network productivity could weaken if fixed\ncosts remain unchanged\nOpportunity\nDigital revenue mix rose to 35.1%\nHigher mix of scalable channels can lift margin\nand improve customer data capture\nOpportunity\nInventory days fell from 74 to 61\nBetter working capital discipline creates room for\nseasonal assortment investment\nOpportunity\nPrivate-label mix reached 21%\nMargin expansion and differentiation potential\nboth improve\n5. Leadership Questions for Review\n• Should Northstar reduce dependence on paid acquisition and prioritize CRM, loyalty, and referral-led\ngrowth?\n• Which store cohorts require format redesign, local assortment changes, or selective consolidation?\n• How aggressively should the company expand private-label categories while preserving quality\nperception?\n• Can digital fulfillment advantages be translated into differentiated in-store pickup and omnichannel\nexperience?\n\n\n=== GENERAL ===\n\n                      Return ONLY valid JSON in this exact schema:\n                      {\n                        \"executive_summary\": [\n                          {\n                            \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n                            \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\", \"<citation2>\"]\n                          }\n                        ],\n                        \"top_risks\": [\n                          {\n                            \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n                            \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n                          }\n                        ],\n                        \"top_opportunities\": [\n                          {\n                            \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n                            \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n                          }\n                        ],\n                        \"recommended_actions\": [\n                          {\n                            \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n                            \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n                          }\n                        ],\n                        \"supporting_evidence\": [\n                          {\n                            \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n                            \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n                          }\n                        ]\n                      }\n\n                      Constraints:\n                      - executive_summary: max 2 bullets\n              