rt.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview\n- Leadership should view the quarter as operationally solid but strategically mixed sample_report_p1_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview\n\nTop Risks\n- Store network productivity could weaken if fixed costs remain unchanged due to declining Tier-2 store traffic sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions\n- Growth may become less efficient unless acquisition mix shifts toward retention and organic demand due to increased paid media CAC sample_report_p1_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview\n\nTop Opportunities\n- Higher mix of scalable channels can lift margin and improve customer data capture due to increased digital revenue mix sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions\n- Better working capital discipline creates room for seasonal assortment investment due to reduced inventory days sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions\n- Margin expansion and differentiation potential both improve due to increased private-label mix sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions\n\nSupporting Evidence\n- Digital revenue mix rose to 35.1%, and private-label penetration reached 21% of revenue sample_report_p1_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions\n- Inventory days fell from 74 to 61, and customer acquisition cost increased by 19.8% sample_report_p1_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions", "prompts": {"system_prompt": "\nYou are a senior strategy consultant preparing a CXO briefing.\n\nYour output must be:\n- concise\n- evidence-grounded\n- high signal, low fluff\n- suitable for senior leadership\n\nRules:\n- Use only the provided context.\n- Do not invent facts.\n- Every bullet MUST copy the citation label EXACTLY as shown in the evidence, including the square brackets.\n\n  Correct example:\n    [sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | table]\n\n  Incorrect examples:\n    sample_report_p2_c0\n    sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf\n\n- Prefer compression over completeness.\n- Do not restate the same evidence twice.\n- If evidence is incomplete, say so briefly.\n- Keep the full response under 220 words.\n- Use short bullets, not long paragraphs.\n\nCritical grounding rules:\n- Do NOT convert open questions into firm recommendations.\n- Do NOT convert implications, risks, or opportunities into actions unless the context explicitly supports an action.\n- If the evidence only suggests a hypothesis, watch item, or leadership question, preserve that uncertainty.\n- Use softer wording when needed, such as:\n  - \"Management should evaluate whether...\"\n  - \"Leadership should consider...\"\n  - \"A watch area is...\"\n- If the context does not clearly support recommended actions, return an empty recommended_actions list.\n- If a statement is only partially supported, prefer narrower and more literal wording.\n- Do not introduce management advice, evaluation language, or decision-oriented framing unless the user explicitly asks for recommendations or the context explicitly states such guidance.\n- For descriptive questions, keep the answer descriptive rather than prescriptive.\n- If the question asks to identify, compare, summarize, or distinguish, do not add action-oriented language.\n\n", "user_prompt": "\nUser Question:\nWhat evidence-backed recommendations should management act on immediately?\n\nStructured Evidence:\n=== EXECUTIVE_OVERVIEW ===\n- [sample_report_p1_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.1 | executive_overview]\nSection Type: executive_overview\nQuarterly Strategic Review — Northstar Retail\nGroup\nSample leadership report for testing a PDF → extraction → chunking → retrieval → executive-summary\npipeline\n1. Executive Overview\nNorthstar Retail Group closed Q2 FY2026 with revenue of $128.4M, up 11.7% year over year, driven by\nstrong digital channel growth and improved premium-category conversion. Gross margin expanded to\n38.6% from 36.9% in the prior-year quarter, supported by lower freight costs and better inventory mix.\nHowever, management noted emerging pressure in same-store traffic across Tier-2 locations and higher\ncustomer acquisition costs in paid media.\nLeadership should view the quarter as operationally solid but strategically mixed: the company is\ndemonstrating resilience in e-commerce and private-label performance, while store productivity and\nmarketing efficiency remain the principal watch areas for the next two quarters.\n2. Performance Summary\nMetric\nQ2 FY2025\nQ2 FY2026\nYoY Change\nRevenue ($M)\n114.9\n128.4\n+11.7%\nGross Margin\n36.9%\n38.6%\n+170 bps\nOperating Income ($M)\n12.2\n15.8\n+29.5%\nDigital Revenue Mix\n29.4%\n35.1%\n+570 bps\nCustomer Acquisition Cost ($)\n18.7\n22.4\n+19.8%\nInventory Days\n74\n61\n-13 days\n3. Segment Commentary\nDigital Commerce. Online sales grew 34% year over year, led by repeat purchase behavior in home\norganization and wellness categories. Management attributed the acceleration to improved product\nrecommendation models, mobile checkout simplification, and faster fulfillment SLAs in metro regions.\nPhysical Stores. Store revenue increased only 2%, with strong flagship performance partly offset by\nweaker traffic in smaller-format suburban stores. Basket size improved, but footfall declined 5% in Tier-2\nlocations, suggesting that conversion is improving faster than raw demand.\nPrivate Label. Private-label penetration reached 21% of revenue versus 16% a year earlier. This mix shift\nwas margin-accretive and reduced exposure to third-party pricing volatility.\n4. Strategic Risks and Opportunities\nCategory\nObservation\nImplication\nRisk\nPaid media CAC increased nearly 20% YoY\nGrowth may become less efficient unless\nacquisition mix shifts toward retention and\norganic demand\n\n\n=== LEADERSHIP_QUESTIONS ===\n- [sample_report_p2_c0 | sample_report.pdf | p.2 | leadership_questions]\nSection Type: leadership_questions\nRisk\nTier-2 store traffic declined 5%\nStore network productivity could weaken if fixed\ncosts remain unchanged\nOpportunity\nDigital revenue mix rose to 35.1%\nHigher mix of scalable channels can lift margin\nand improve customer data capture\nOpportunity\nInventory days fell from 74 to 61\nBetter working capital discipline creates room for\nseasonal assortment investment\nOpportunity\nPrivate-label mix reached 21%\nMargin expansion and differentiation potential\nboth improve\n5. Leadership Questions for Review\n• Should Northstar reduce dependence on paid acquisition and prioritize CRM, loyalty, and referral-led\ngrowth?\n• Which store cohorts require format redesign, local assortment changes, or selective consolidation?\n• How aggressively should the company expand private-label categories while preserving quality\nperception?\n• Can digital fulfillment advantages be translated into differentiated in-store pickup and omnichannel\nexperience?\n\n\n=== GENERAL ===\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this exact schema:\n{\n  \"executive_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n      \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\", \"<citation2>\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"top_risks\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n      \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"top_opportunities\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n      \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n      \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"supporting_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"<bullet>\",\n      \"citations\": [\"<citation1>\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nConstraints:\n- executive_summary: max 2 bullets\n- top_risks: max 3 bullets\n- top_opportunities: max 3 bullets\n- recommended_actions: max 3 bullets, but MAY be an empty list if evidence is not explicit\n- supporting_evidence: max 2 bullets\n\nImportant:\n- Use the exact citation labels already present in the evidence.\n- Do not include markdown.\n- Do not wrap JSON in ```json fences.\n- Do not include any text before or after the JSON.\n- recommended_actions must only include actions that are explicitly supported by the evidence.\n- If the evidence contains only leadership questions or implications, do not rewrite them as decided actions.\n- Match the user's intent closely:\n  - if the question is descriptive or comparative, keep the response descriptive/comparative\n  - do not introduce recommendations unless explicitly requested.\n", "formatted_context_chars": 3406}, "trace": {"events": [{"stage": "retrieval", "duration_ms": 72.26, "payload": {"candidate_count": 3, "query_variants": ["What evidence-backed recommendations should management act on immediately?"]}}, {"stage": "reranking", "duration_ms": 14216.06, "payload": {"final_count": 3}}, {"stage": "context_packing", "duration_ms": 0.1, "payload": {"context_chars": 3406}}, {"stage": "generation", "duration_ms": 1845.23, "payload": {"answer_chars": 1745}}, {"stage": "evaluation", "duration_ms": 4639.95, "payload": {"faithfulness_score": 7, "groundedness_score": 7}}]}, "llm_provider": "groq", "llm_model": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile", "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2", "ground_truth": {"relevant_chunk_ids": [], "graded_relevance": {}}, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": null, "completion_tokens": null, "total_tokens": null, "estimated_cost_usd": null}, "evaluation": {"query": "What evidence-backed recommendations should management act on immediately?", "retrieval": {"precision_at_k": "N/A (no labeled relevant_chunk_ids provided)", "recall_at_k": "N/A (no labeled relevant_chunk_ids provided)", "mrr": null, "ndcg_at_k": null}, "faithfulness": {"faithfulness_score": 7, "directly_supported_claims": ["Northstar Retail Group closed Q2 FY2026 with revenue of $128.4M, up 11.7% year over year", "Leadership should view the quarter as op